#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186188003 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186188296 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "7447ccfe-83a7-59d4-8386-c74a3ab47b89" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Expected Value of a Continuous Random Variable From a Joint Distribution"}] :question/id #uuid "f32f96bc-b02a-54fe-b370-8a384c6ae67e" :question/math-academy-id "e-10102" :question/problem "Let $X$ and $Y$ be two continuous random variables with the joint probability density function\n\n![](images/f5/f5e1e2931a6ad6c4b5751d67e325cc0aca6cbae85200e5d2fbd6f60ea28c899c.svg)\n\nFind the expected value of $Y.$" :question/worked-solution "The marginal density function for $Y$ when $y \\geq 1$ is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{Y}(y) & ={\\int }_{1}^{\\infty }\\frac{4}{{x}^{3}{y}^{3}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{{y}^{3}}{lim}_{b\\to \\infty }{\\int }_{1}^{b}\\frac{1}{{x}^{3}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{{y}^{3}}{lim}_{b\\to \\infty }{[-\\frac{1}{2{x}^{2}}]}_{1}^{b} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{{y}^{3}}{lim}_{b\\to \\infty }(\\frac{1}{2}-\\frac{1}{2{b}^{2}}) \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{{y}^{3}}(\\frac{1}{2}-0) \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{{y}^{3}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the full expression for $f_Y(y)$ is given by\n\n![](images/4d/4dcb0094faeee6f3f155eb2e7a87c24cfb976c3f860f30b13cd7da61512544b2.svg)\n\nFinally, the  expected value of $Y$ is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[Y] & ={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }y\\cdot {f}_{Y}(y)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{\\infty }y\\cdot \\frac{2}{{y}^{3}}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =2{lim}_{b\\to \\infty }{\\int }_{1}^{b}\\frac{1}{{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =2{lim}_{b\\to \\infty }{[-\\frac{1}{y}]}_{1}^{b} \\\\  & =2{lim}_{b\\to \\infty }(1-\\frac{1}{b}) \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186188211 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186188276 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "1892c89c-8343-57ff-8c7e-e6edb35bb7c6" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Expected Value of a Discrete Random Variable From a Joint Distribution"}] :question/id #uuid "136ceff6-b85b-5686-a69b-5d39ff70d3dd" :question/math-academy-id "e-9191" :question/problem "Given the joint probability distribution for two discrete random variables $X$ and $Y$ below, find $\\textrm{E}[4X-3Y].$\n\n| $f$ | $Y=0$ | $Y=1$ | $Y=3$ | $Y=5$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=-1$ | $0.1$ | $0.1$ | $0.05$ | $0.1$ |\n| $X=2$ | $0.1$ | $0.05$ | $0.1$ | $0.1$ |\n| $X=4$ | $0.1$ | $0.05$ | $0.05$ | $0.1$ |" :question/worked-solution "Recall that the marginal distribution for $X$ corresponds to the row totals, and the marginal distribution for $Y$ corresponds to the column totals.\n\n| $f$ | $Y=0$ | $Y=1$ | $Y=3$ | $Y=5$ | $f_X$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=-1$ | $0.1$ | $0.1$ | $0.05$ | $0.1$ | $0.35$ |\n| $X=2$ | $0.1$ | $0.05$ | $0.1$ | $0.1$ | $0.35$ |\n| $X=4$ | $0.1$ | $0.05$ | $0.05$ | $0.1$ | $0.3$ |\n| $f_Y$ | $0.3$ | $0.2$ | $0.2$ | $0.3$ | $1$ |\n\nTherefore,  the probability mass functions for  $X$ and $Y$ are given by the following tables:\n\n<table align=\"center\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<th>\n<table align=\"center\" cellpadding=\"10\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" width=\"30\">$x$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$-1$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$2$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$4$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" width=\"30\">$f_X(x)$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0.35$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0.35$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0.3$</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<p></p></th>\n<th width=\"50\"></th>\n<th>\n<table align=\"center\" cellpadding=\"10\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" width=\"30\">$y$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$1$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$3$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$5$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" width=\"30\">$f_Y(y)$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0.3$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0.2$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0.2$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0.3$</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<p></p></th>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n\nNow, we can compute the expected values for $X$ and $Y{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[X] & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{x}_{i}\\,{f}_{X}({x}_{i}) \\\\  & =(-1)\\cdot 0.35+2\\cdot 0.35+4\\cdot 0.3 \\\\  & =-0.35+0.7+1.2 \\\\  & =1.55\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[Y] & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{y}_{i}\\,{f}_{Y}({y}_{i}) \\\\  & =0\\cdot 0.3+1\\cdot 0.2+3\\cdot 0.2+5\\cdot 0.3 \\\\  & =0+0.2+0.6+1.5 \\\\  & =2.3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, using the properties of expectation, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[4X-3Y] & =4\\text{E}[X]-3\\,\\text{E}[Y] \\\\  & =4(1.55)-3(2.3) \\\\  & =6.2-6.9 \\\\  & =-0.7.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186188537 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186188276 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "1892c89c-8343-57ff-8c7e-e6edb35bb7c6" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Expected Value of a Discrete Random Variable From a Joint Distribution"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "98bb64f7-641f-59a7-a812-6d77dc3d0d4e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186185503} {:answer/id #uuid "a941f419-0d37-591c-995d-8af3a83343be" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186185504} {:answer/id #uuid "e90482ed-b3a5-55c1-af51-365cee2dbd66" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1.15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186185505} {:answer/id #uuid "527c70d1-ccf1-5859-a3e4-1c9cb172ee18" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1.7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186185506} {:answer/id #uuid "57c5a184-30c4-532e-95e5-184b1d37149f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1.5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186185507}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "98bb64f7-641f-59a7-a812-6d77dc3d0d4e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186185503} :answer-field/id #uuid "6dbd4740-7ca3-58ee-8130-82cc83c7176b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186185502}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "eec76c44-d392-55db-8b1d-f24621c0b38c" :question/math-academy-id "q-110404" :question/problem "Given the joint probability distribution for two discrete random variables $X$ and $Y$ below, find $\\text{E}[5X-2Y].$\n\n| $f$ | $Y=0$ | $Y=1$ | $Y=2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=0$ | $0.05$ | $0.1$ | $0.25$ |\n| $X=1$ | $0.25$ | $0.15$ | $0.2$ |" :question/requires-calculator true :question/worked-solution "Recall that the marginal distribution for $X$ corresponds to the row totals, and the marginal distribution for $Y$ corresponds to the column totals.\n\n| $f$ | $Y=0$ | $Y=1$ | $Y=2$ | ${f}_{X}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=0$ | $0.05$ | $0.1$ | $0.25$ | $0.4$ |\n| $X=1$ | $0.25$ | $0.15$ | $0.2$ | $0.6$ |\n| ${f}_{Y}$ | $0.3$ | $0.25$ | $0.45$ | $1$ |\n\nTherefore,  the probability mass functions for  $X$ and $Y$ are given by the following tables:\n\n<table align=\"center\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<th>\n<table align=\"center\" cellpadding=\"10\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" width=\"30\">$x$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$1$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" width=\"30\">${f}_{X}(x)$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0.4$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0.6$</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<p></p></th>\n<th width=\"50\"></th>\n<th>\n<table align=\"center\" cellpadding=\"10\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" width=\"30\">$y$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$1$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$2$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" width=\"30\">${f}_{Y}(y)$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0.3$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0.25$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0.45$</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<p></p></th>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n\nNow, we can compute the expected values for $X$ and $Y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[X] & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{x}_{i}\\,{f}_{X}({x}_{i}) \\\\  & =0\\cdot 0.4+1\\cdot 0.6 \\\\  & =0+0.6 \\\\  & =0.6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[Y] & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{y}_{i}\\,{f}_{Y}({y}_{i}) \\\\  & =0\\cdot 0.3+1\\cdot 0.25+2\\cdot 0.45 \\\\  & =0+0.25+0.9 \\\\  & =1.15.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, using the properties of expectation, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[5X-2Y] & =5\\,\\text{E}[X]-2\\,\\text{E}[Y] \\\\  & =5(0.6)-2(1.15) \\\\  & =3-2.3 \\\\  & =0.7.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186478429 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186188276 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "1892c89c-8343-57ff-8c7e-e6edb35bb7c6" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Expected Value of a Discrete Random Variable From a Joint Distribution"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "101d5428-dcc7-5dee-b252-67e17bed80f8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477760} {:answer/id #uuid "16a4eb8e-83f0-5ca3-8940-87a0cab24cd8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.55" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477775} {:answer/id #uuid "30ee8457-b304-5878-aa08-b58c2b7f4411" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477826} {:answer/id #uuid "5c889d5b-91ba-5144-b5a7-d6ec1b10c9ca" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477924} {:answer/id #uuid "8f5fc3ca-7aec-5456-9d54-565da8c428c8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.45" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186478021}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "16a4eb8e-83f0-5ca3-8940-87a0cab24cd8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.55" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477775} :answer-field/id #uuid "e3534f0e-3d63-59cf-a199-e7560f733af5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186478355}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "9b844eb7-526d-53c8-86e0-b25751033892" :question/math-academy-id "q-143561" :question/problem "Given the joint probability distribution for two discrete random variables $X$ and $Y$ below, find $\\text{E}[X].$\n\n| $f$ | $Y=1$ | $Y=2$ | $Y=3$ | $Y=4$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=0$ | $0.2$ | $0.05$ | $0.15$ | $0.05$ |\n| $X=1$ | $0.05$ | $0.1$ | $0.25$ | $0.15$ |" :question/worked-solution "Recall that the marginal distribution for $X$ corresponds to the row totals, and the marginal distribution for $Y$ corresponds to the column totals.\n\n| $f(x,y)$ | $Y=1$ | $Y=2$ | $Y=3$ | $Y=4$ | ${f}_{X}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=0$ | $0.2$ | $0.05$ | $0.15$ | $0.05$ | $0.45$ |\n| $X=1$ | $0.05$ | $0.1$ | $0.25$ | $0.15$ | $0.55$ |\n| ${f}_{Y}$ | $…$ | $…$ | $…$ | $…$ | $1$ |\n\nTherefore, the probability mass function for  $X$ is given by the following table:\n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $1$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| ${f}_{X}(x)$ | $0.45$ | $0.55$ |\n\nFinally, the  expected value of $X$ is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[X] & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{x}_{i}\\,{f}_{X}({x}_{i}) \\\\  & =0\\cdot 0.45+1\\cdot 0.55 \\\\  & =0+0.55 \\\\  & =0.55.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186478433 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186188276 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "1892c89c-8343-57ff-8c7e-e6edb35bb7c6" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Expected Value of a Discrete Random Variable From a Joint Distribution"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0647397e-d566-5ed1-8a7c-3ecc46633591" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477746} {:answer/id #uuid "81b1858d-2bfd-5b49-82ba-6a675c4e406a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186478004} {:answer/id #uuid "a5f3a3f4-d817-5dcf-8713-1436149c861f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186478054} {:answer/id #uuid "d33cda86-ecab-52b7-98a9-9a05e5761f8f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186478153} {:answer/id #uuid "fef005f2-c5c6-5d6f-a606-7dc76406f94e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1.3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186478243}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a5f3a3f4-d817-5dcf-8713-1436149c861f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186478054} :answer-field/id #uuid "743a2df1-2675-5f54-8ed7-9aa8c9d1a1f3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186478305}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "adc77faf-eae7-5c2f-8af1-752f3d590d9a" :question/math-academy-id "q-143564" :question/problem "Given the joint probability distribution for two discrete random variables $X$ and $Y$ below, find $\\text{E}[X].$\n\n| $f$ | $Y=1$ | $Y=2$ | $Y=3$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=-1$ | $0.05$ | $0.05$ | $0.2$ |\n| $X=1$ | $0.15$ | $0.1$ | $0.15$ |\n| $X=3$ | $0.15$ | $0.05$ | $0.1$ |" :question/worked-solution "Recall that the marginal distribution for $X$ corresponds to the row totals, and the marginal distribution for $Y$ corresponds to the column totals.\n\n| $f(x,y)$ | $Y=1$ | $Y=2$ | $Y=3$ | ${f}_{X}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=-1$ | $0.05$ | $0.05$ | $0.2$ | $0.3$ |\n| $X=1$ | $0.15$ | $0.1$ | $0.15$ | $0.4$ |\n| $X=3$ | $0.15$ | $0.05$ | $0.1$ | $0.3$ |\n| ${f}_{Y}$ | $…$ | $…$ | $…$ | $1$ |\n\nTherefore, the probability mass function for  $X$ is given by the following table:\n\n| $x$ | $-1$ | $1$ | $3$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| ${f}_{X}(x)$ | $0.3$ | $0.4$ | $0.3$ |\n\nFinally, the  expected value of $X$ is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[X] & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{x}_{i}\\,{f}_{X}({x}_{i}) \\\\  & =(-1)\\cdot 0.3+1\\cdot 0.4+3\\cdot 0.3 \\\\  & =-0.3+0.4+0.9 \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186478400 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186188276 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "1892c89c-8343-57ff-8c7e-e6edb35bb7c6" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Expected Value of a Discrete Random Variable From a Joint Distribution"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0eb8ab13-7569-5d22-82e5-e5660fbcb4e0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1.8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477759} {:answer/id #uuid "3ebc2abe-8b1c-5e51-8f14-19b4dc52b753" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1.3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477852} {:answer/id #uuid "481ad469-d297-52a0-96dc-467534b3627d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2.1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477876} {:answer/id #uuid "ba2e5652-5dff-59c0-a99c-2b960a2a5338" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186478099} {:answer/id #uuid "e70b39f1-1ae1-53c9-a657-8f47a64596ea" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186478192}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ba2e5652-5dff-59c0-a99c-2b960a2a5338" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186478099} :answer-field/id #uuid "fc1b00f2-ed27-5cfb-9ff3-8ef3f65eb0c7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186478365}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "48136ec2-d65d-59a7-87bb-a7d2f39b6298" :question/math-academy-id "q-143570" :question/problem "Given the joint probability distribution for two discrete random variables $X$ and $Y$ below, find $\\text{E}[Y-X].$\n\n| $f$ | $Y=-1$ | $Y=1$ | $Y=2$ | $Y=4$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=1$ | $0.05$ | $0.1$ | $0.2$ | $0.15$ |\n| $X=2$ | $0.2$ | $0.05$ | $0.15$ | $0.1$ |" :question/worked-solution "Recall that the marginal distribution for $X$ corresponds to the row totals, and the marginal distribution for $Y$ corresponds to the column totals.\n\n| $f$ | $Y=-1$ | $Y=1$ | $Y=2$ | $Y=4$ | ${f}_{X}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=1$ | $0.05$ | $0.1$ | $0.2$ | $0.15$ | $0.5$ |\n| $X=2$ | $0.2$ | $0.05$ | $0.15$ | $0.1$ | $0.5$ |\n| ${f}_{Y}$ | $0.25$ | $0.15$ | $0.35$ | $0.25$ | $1$ |\n\nTherefore,  the probability mass functions for  $X$ and $Y$ are given by the following tables:\n\n<table align=\"center\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<th>\n<table align=\"center\" cellpadding=\"10\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" width=\"30\">$x$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$1$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$2$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" width=\"30\">${f}_{X}(x)$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0.5$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0.5$</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<p></p></th>\n<th width=\"50\"></th>\n<th>\n<table align=\"center\" cellpadding=\"10\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" width=\"30\">$y$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$-1$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$1$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$2$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$4$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" width=\"30\">${f}_{Y}(y)$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0.25$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0.15$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0.35$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0.25$</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<p></p></th>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n\nNow, we can compute the expected values for $X$ and $Y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[X] & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{x}_{i}\\,{f}_{X}({x}_{i}) \\\\  & =1\\cdot 0.5+2\\cdot 0.5 \\\\  & =0.5+1 \\\\  & =1.5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[Y] & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{y}_{i}\\,{f}_{Y}({y}_{i}) \\\\  & =(-1)\\cdot 0.25+1\\cdot 0.15+2\\cdot 0.35+4\\cdot 0.25 \\\\  & =-0.25+0.15+0.7+1 \\\\  & =1.6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, using the properties of expectation, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[Y-X] & =\\text{E}[Y]-\\,\\text{E}[X] \\\\  & =1.6-1.5 \\\\  & =0.1.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186478440 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186188276 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "1892c89c-8343-57ff-8c7e-e6edb35bb7c6" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Expected Value of a Discrete Random Variable From a Joint Distribution"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "17ecec0d-732c-5414-845c-7ef17e8b344f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2.7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477776} {:answer/id #uuid "1e2dcf8d-92bd-5128-b063-32e97dd8d44d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "11.55" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477790} {:answer/id #uuid "1ef98f0f-0ba4-5459-8e2a-c224ee049531" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1.95" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477793} {:answer/id #uuid "7178c7ab-c7ee-54b4-b951-cfe9e55b1ef6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4.3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477975} {:answer/id #uuid "96f418aa-e1b5-5d46-8deb-e291d0bcaa15" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2.05" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186478029}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "17ecec0d-732c-5414-845c-7ef17e8b344f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2.7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477776} :answer-field/id #uuid "8c8c9024-afad-538f-a0cd-83bc4e49af33" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186478318}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "b990b80d-8f23-5220-a540-72805037f053" :question/math-academy-id "q-143571" :question/problem "Given the joint probability distribution for two discrete random variables $X$ and $Y$ below, find $\\text{E}[2X-3Y].$\n\n| $f$ | $Y=2$ | $Y=3$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=1$ | $0.25$ | $0.1$ |\n| $X=2$ | $0.2$ | $0.15$ |\n| $X=4$ | $0.15$ | $0.15$ |" :question/worked-solution "Recall that the marginal distribution for $X$ corresponds to the row totals, and the marginal distribution for $Y$ corresponds to the column totals.\n\n| $f$ | $Y=2$ | $Y=3$ | ${f}_{X}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=1$ | $0.25$ | $0.1$ | $0.35$ |\n| $X=2$ | $0.2$ | $0.15$ | $0.35$ |\n| $X=4$ | $0.15$ | $0.15$ | $0.3$ |\n| ${f}_{Y}$ | $0.6$ | $0.4$ | $1$ |\n\nTherefore,  the probability mass functions for  $X$ and $Y$ are given by the following tables:\n\n<table align=\"center\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<th>\n<table align=\"center\" cellpadding=\"10\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" width=\"30\">$x$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$1$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$2$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$4$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" width=\"30\">${f}_{X}(x)$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0.35$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0.35$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0.3$</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<p></p></th>\n<th width=\"50\"></th>\n<th>\n<table align=\"center\" cellpadding=\"10\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" width=\"30\">$y$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$2$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$3$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" width=\"30\">${f}_{Y}(y)$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0.6$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0.4$</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<p></p></th>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n\nNow, we can compute the expected values for $X$ and $Y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[X] & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{x}_{i}\\,{f}_{X}({x}_{i}) \\\\  & =1\\cdot 0.35+2\\cdot 0.35+4\\cdot 0.3 \\\\  & =0.35+0.7+1.2 \\\\  & =2.25\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[Y] & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{y}_{i}\\,{f}_{Y}({y}_{i}) \\\\  & =2\\cdot 0.6+3\\cdot 0.4 \\\\  & =1.2+1.2 \\\\  & =2.4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, using the properties of expectation, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[2X-3Y] & =2\\,\\text{E}[X]-3\\,\\text{E}[Y] \\\\  & =2(2.25)-3(2.4) \\\\  & =4.5-7.2 \\\\  & =-2.7.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186478451 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186188296 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "7447ccfe-83a7-59d4-8386-c74a3ab47b89" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Expected Value of a Continuous Random Variable From a Joint Distribution"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2582ad56-e0fc-5e45-a724-0bf543eb47b6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477809} {:answer/id #uuid "6d662136-b6b4-51b7-b84c-28e07ae855b7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477962} {:answer/id #uuid "926d3769-d90a-5427-ba8d-6e61ed8728c7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186478024} {:answer/id #uuid "f7a07fa4-4e2c-5f65-b0cc-82609ae32a36" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186478228} {:answer/id #uuid "f8b6ba3f-5d68-5219-9887-1a4d3342335a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186478231}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6d662136-b6b4-51b7-b84c-28e07ae855b7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477962} :answer-field/id #uuid "456ccbaa-8e08-50d2-a659-91ea1be33e5d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186478272}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "dc0d3274-ca1e-5ab4-bb51-ab607148446e" :question/math-academy-id "q-143580" :question/problem "Let $X$ and $Y$ be two continuous random variables with the joint probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x,y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}xy, & 0\\le x\\le 2,\\,0\\le y\\le 1, \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nGiven that $\\text{E}[Y]=\\frac{2}{3},$ find $\\text{E}[X+Y].$" :question/worked-solution "We're given $\\text{E}[Y].$ So, we first need to compute $\\text{E}[X].$\n\nThe marginal density function for $X$ when $0\\le x\\le 2$ is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{X}(x) & ={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}xy\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =x{[\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2}]}_{y=0}^{y=1} \\\\  & =\\frac{x}{2}(1-0) \\\\  & =\\frac{x}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the  expected value of $X$ is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[X] & ={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }x\\,{f}_{X}(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}x\\cdot \\frac{x}{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{2}{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{[\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}]}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}(8-0) \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[X+Y] & =\\text{E}[X]+\\text{E}[Y] \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}+\\frac{4}{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{6}{3} \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186478427 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186188296 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "7447ccfe-83a7-59d4-8386-c74a3ab47b89" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Expected Value of a Continuous Random Variable From a Joint Distribution"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "12570832-3b6e-5b6a-a287-f07c08e82469" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477767} {:answer/id #uuid "49cebb4d-b38a-5cf8-b82c-e24d65ce5841" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477881} {:answer/id #uuid "7dd03053-40a1-5247-bf67-f15a373a1271" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477993} {:answer/id #uuid "a6f16c4e-2ef7-5efd-a643-9353ecd1c160" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186478057} {:answer/id #uuid "e2b0f5cc-c808-51bb-83ca-aa8b0db3fc8f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186478182}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e2b0f5cc-c808-51bb-83ca-aa8b0db3fc8f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186478182} :answer-field/id #uuid "6d767f87-00d4-53d3-9572-4ca534bc85cc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186478300}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "9118031b-d926-55ed-8f7f-1b50c43555cf" :question/math-academy-id "q-143581" :question/problem "Let $X$ and $Y$ be two continuous random variables with the joint probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x,y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{y\\sqrt{x}}{3}, & 0\\le x\\le 1,\\,0\\le y\\le 3, \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nGiven that $\\text{E}[X]=\\frac{3}{5},$ find $\\text{E}[5X-Y].$" :question/worked-solution "We're given $\\text{E}[X].$ So, we first need to compute $\\text{E}[Y].$\n\nThe marginal density function for $Y$ when $0\\le y\\le 3$ is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{Y}(y) & ={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{y\\sqrt{x}}{3}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{y}{3}{[\\frac{2}{3}{x}^{3/2}]}_{x=0}^{x=1} \\\\  & =\\frac{y}{3}(\\frac{2}{3}-0) \\\\  & =\\frac{2y}{9}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the  expected value of $Y$ is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[Y] & ={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }y\\,{f}_{Y}(y)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}y\\cdot \\frac{2y}{9}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{9}{\\int }_{0}^{3}{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{9}{[\\frac{{y}^{3}}{3}]}_{0}^{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{9}(9-0) \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[5X-Y] & =5\\,\\text{E}[X]+(-1)\\,\\text{E}[Y] \\\\  & =5(\\frac{3}{5})+(-1)(2) \\\\  & =3-2 \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186478463 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186188296 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "7447ccfe-83a7-59d4-8386-c74a3ab47b89" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Expected Value of a Continuous Random Variable From a Joint Distribution"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2254d91b-2958-56f7-a120-27c4c74d4b64" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{11}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477802} {:answer/id #uuid "4ad94bc4-7977-503e-8e74-9824f2c3dd66" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{11}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477884} {:answer/id #uuid "67b691a4-53c4-583b-a2ee-14c4b487753a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{11}{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477944} {:answer/id #uuid "c3855371-283d-591c-8921-54d6156c7ab5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186478123} {:answer/id #uuid "de2f4f3e-77a6-5b13-b71d-314248ef5d65" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186478172}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2254d91b-2958-56f7-a120-27c4c74d4b64" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{11}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477802} :answer-field/id #uuid "d18c8ecd-2d64-503b-a8ad-b4276195c72b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186478342}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "faa5f199-79d7-5c93-85da-fb2ae026c8e7" :question/math-academy-id "q-143582" :question/problem "Let $X$ and $Y$ be two continuous random variables with the joint probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x,y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{x}^{2}+y}{21}, & -3\\le x\\le 3,\\,0\\le y\\le 1, \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nGiven that $\\text{E}[X]=0,$ find $\\text{E}[3X+7Y].$" :question/worked-solution "We're given $\\text{E}[X].$ So, we first need to compute $\\text{E}[Y].$\n\nThe marginal density function for $Y$ when $0\\le y\\le 1$ is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{Y}(y) & ={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-3}^{3}\\frac{{x}^{2}+y}{21}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{21}{[\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}+xy]}_{x=-3}^{x=3} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{21}[(\\frac{{3}^{3}}{3}+3y)-(\\frac{(-3)^{3}}{3}-3y)] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{21}[18+6y] \\\\  & =\\frac{2(3+y)}{7}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the  expected value of $Y$ is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[Y] & ={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }y\\,{f}_{Y}(y)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}y\\cdot \\frac{2(3+y)}{7}.\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{7}{\\int }_{0}^{1}3y+{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{7}{[\\frac{3{y}^{2}}{2}+\\frac{{y}^{3}}{3}]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{7}(\\frac{3}{2}+\\frac{1}{3}-0) \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{7}\\cdot \\frac{11}{6} \\\\  & =\\frac{11}{21}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[3X+7Y] & =3\\,\\text{E}[X]+7\\,\\text{E}[Y] \\\\  & =3(0)+7(\\frac{11}{21}) \\\\  & =0+\\frac{11}{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{11}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186478374 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186188296 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "7447ccfe-83a7-59d4-8386-c74a3ab47b89" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Expected Value of a Continuous Random Variable From a Joint Distribution"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "19b043ff-ed32-5ad4-8ebf-e2dbbeee6aa9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{17}{10}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477780} {:answer/id #uuid "6fbdc895-0ad3-573a-b041-364e600b7833" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{97}{70}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477967} {:answer/id #uuid "76807ce6-5aeb-5a78-bae9-dad2221d3b3e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{113}{70}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477983} {:answer/id #uuid "bbe4e1b2-7e7c-587d-9be9-d85905eba39c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{16}{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186478102} {:answer/id #uuid "bd5e3592-112b-5b2a-a863-26e667cdaf7f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{9}{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186478104}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "19b043ff-ed32-5ad4-8ebf-e2dbbeee6aa9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{17}{10}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477780} :answer-field/id #uuid "3a2ff3fa-3979-54c7-9c20-3011a115fa47" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186478271}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "0eaad2fb-faea-5de0-88f1-158f02ba672a" :question/math-academy-id "q-149609" :question/problem "Let $X$ and $Y$ be two continuous random variables with the joint probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x,y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{6}{7}(x+\\sqrt{y}), & 0\\le x\\le 1,\\,0\\le y\\le 1, \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nGiven that $\\text{E}[X]=\\frac{4}{7},$ find $\\text{E}[2X+Y].$" :question/worked-solution "We're given $\\text{E}[X].$ So, we first need to compute $\\text{E}[Y].$\n\nThe marginal density function for $Y$ when $0\\le y\\le 1$ is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{Y}(y) & ={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{6}{7}(x+\\sqrt{y})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{6}{7}{[\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{2}+x\\sqrt{y}]}_{x=0}^{x=1} \\\\  & =\\frac{6}{7}(\\frac{1}{2}+\\sqrt{y}) \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{7}(2\\sqrt{y}+1).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the  expected value of $Y$ is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[Y] & ={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }y\\,{f}_{Y}(y)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}y\\cdot \\frac{3}{7}(2\\sqrt{y}+1)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{7}{\\int }_{0}^{1}(2{y}^{3/2}+y)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{7}{[\\frac{4}{5}{y}^{5/2}+\\frac{1}{2}{y}^{2}]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{7}(\\frac{4}{5}+\\frac{1}{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{39}{70}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[2X+Y] & =2\\,\\text{E}[X]+\\text{E}[Y] \\\\  & =2(\\frac{4}{7})+(\\frac{39}{70}) \\\\  & =\\frac{80+39}{70} \\\\  & =\\frac{17}{10}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186478405 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186188296 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "7447ccfe-83a7-59d4-8386-c74a3ab47b89" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Expected Value of a Continuous Random Variable From a Joint Distribution"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4447cc98-6743-5c8b-ae0d-f98d22239d3e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477863} {:answer/id #uuid "6296064a-90d1-5369-b44b-518fa6f48fca" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{8}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477938} {:answer/id #uuid "b2bdf207-5309-5c13-8d6f-2a82165c7979" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{9}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186478086} {:answer/id #uuid "daf607a2-d3a0-519f-ab73-cf8bd7135eea" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{11}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186478164} {:answer/id #uuid "e4406152-e5b4-5362-b7c4-2fdf2a10e810" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{9}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186478185}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6296064a-90d1-5369-b44b-518fa6f48fca" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{8}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477938} :answer-field/id #uuid "08f42a5d-307f-5689-a28c-cb44ddd1c806" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186478248}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "5aba2c2c-b7e8-572a-a813-c98db854f118" :question/math-academy-id "q-149614" :question/problem "Let $X$ and $Y$ be two continuous random variables with the joint probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x,y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{5}(x+2y), & 1\\le x\\le 2,\\,0\\le y\\le 1, \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nGiven that $\\text{E}[Y]=\\frac{17}{30},$ find $\\text{E}[X+2Y].$" :question/worked-solution "We're given $\\text{E}[Y].$ So, we first need to compute $\\text{E}[X].$\n\nThe marginal density function for $X$ when $1\\le x\\le 2$ is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{X}(x) & ={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{2}{5}(x+2y)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{5}{[xy+{y}^{2}]}_{y=0}^{y=1} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{5}(x+1-0) \\\\  & =\\frac{2(x+1)}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the  expected value of $X$ is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[X] & ={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }x\\,{f}_{X}(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}x\\cdot \\frac{2(x+1)}{5}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{5}{\\int }_{1}^{2}({x}^{2}+x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{5}{[\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}+\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}]}_{1}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{5}(\\frac{8}{3}+2-\\frac{1}{3}-\\frac{1}{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{23}{15}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[X+2Y] & =\\text{E}[X]+2\\text{E}[Y] \\\\  & =\\frac{23}{15}+2(\\frac{17}{30}) \\\\  & =\\frac{23}{15}+\\frac{17}{15} \\\\  & =\\frac{40}{15} \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
